    "observed_command": "Yeah, I tried stock vllm and the ds4_v8.md image (0.11.2.dev279+eldritch.enlightenment.2226f26.b12x15cd38c.fi25dd814.cu132.20260629). I'm using that to run DS4F TP2 (without docker), with about a ~10% loss from the wiki numbers, because of the 300W PL and PCIe4x16, which is why I was expecting to be a little slower than your numbers. I realized I hadn't looked at the model discussions on HF (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Qwen3.6-27B-NVFP4/discussions). Looks like lots of the same issue, and other people reporting it is the same speed as FP8. The only people reporting higher tps numbers don't share... VLLM_USE_B12X_FP8_GEMM=1 and --block-size 64 gets it to start, but it crashes with File \"/opt/sglang/ds4-v8/lib/python3.12/site-packages/b12x/attention/paged/planner.py\", line 889, in create_paged_plan (EngineCore pid=96475) ERROR 07-10 23:12:01 [core.py:1231] raise ValueError( (EngineCore pid=96475) ERROR 07-10 23:12:01 [core.py:1231] ValueError: paged plan page_table width=4100 exceeds workspace capacity 4096",
